Q: How can I get the Bluetooth device battery percentage using PowerShell on Windows? A: <p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/71736070/how-to-get-bluetooth-device-battery-percentage-using-powershell-on-windows#comment127757728_71737852">Paulo Amaral's comment</a> is indeed the answer.</p>
<p>The code below will provide you with a command you can reuse to query the battery state of your device:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Get-PnpDevice -FriendlyName &quot;*&lt;Device Name&gt;*&quot; | ForEach-Object {
    $local:test = $_ |
    Get-PnpDeviceProperty -KeyName '{104EA319-6EE2-4701-BD47-8DDBF425BBE5} 2' |
        Where Type -ne Empty;
    if ($test) {
        &quot;To query battery for $($_.FriendlyName), run the following:&quot;
        &quot;    Get-PnpDeviceProperty -InstanceId '$($test.InstanceId)' -KeyName '{104EA319-6EE2-4701-BD47-8DDBF425BBE5} 2' | % Data&quot;
        &quot;&quot;
        &quot;The result will look like this:&quot;;
        Get-PnpDeviceProperty -InstanceId $($test.InstanceId) -KeyName '{104EA319-6EE2-4701-BD47-8DDBF425BBE5} 2' | % Data
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>For my <code>&lt;Headset&gt;</code> device, the output looked similar to:</p>
<blockquote>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>To query battery for &lt;Headset&gt;, run the following:
Get-PnpDeviceProperty -InstanceId 'BTHENUM\{0000####-0000-####-####-############}_VID&amp;########_PID&amp;####\#&amp;########&amp;#&amp;############_#########' -KeyName '{104EA319-6EE2-4701-BD47-8DDBF425BBE5} 2'

The result will look like this:
90
</code></pre>
</blockquote>

